## 题目
The (shaded) area under the graph of $y = f(x)$ between $x = 1$ and $x = 2$ is given to be $1$.

![[Image/97-Q1H-fig1.jpg]]

The area under the graph of $y = 2f(3 - x)$ between $x = 1$ and $x = 2$ is therefore
(i) $1$,
(ii) $2$,
(iii) $3$,
(iv) $6$.

## 备注

### 我的备注

### AI备注


## 答案
(ii)

## 解析
We are given that $\int_{1}^{2} f(x) \,\mathrm{d}x = 1$. We need to evaluate the integral

$$\int_{1}^{2} 2f(3 - x) \,\mathrm{d}x$$

Let $u = 3 - x$. Then $\mathrm{d}x = -\mathrm{d}u$. When $x = 1$, $u = 2$; when $x = 2$, $u = 1$. Substituting this into the integral gives

$$\int_{2}^{1} 2f(u) (-\mathrm{d}u) = 2 \int_{1}^{2} f(u) \,\mathrm{d}u$$

Using the given area, this evaluates to $2 \times 1 = 2$. The answer is (ii).
